cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "tnbc-lactate-myeloid: analysis pipeline for lactate-associated myeloid trained states in triple-negative breast cancer"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - name: "[Corresponding author]"
    affiliation: "[Affiliation]"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/[ORCID]"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-01-01"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/<account>/tnbc-lactate-myeloid"
url: "https://github.com/<account>/tnbc-lactate-myeloid"
abstract: >-
  Reproducible pipeline for the study "Lactate-driven trained immunity defines
  prognostically distinct myeloid states in triple-negative breast cancer". It builds
  two directional myeloid gene-programme scores (LT-pro, LT-anti), residualises them on
  an estimate of myeloid abundance, assigns tumours by a deterministic quadrant rule,
  and validates the partition in TCGA-BRCA, METABRIC and GSE176078. All inputs are
  public; no new experimental data were generated.
keywords:
  - trained immunity
  - histone lactylation
  - tumour-associated macrophage
  - triple-negative breast cancer
  - tumour microenvironment
  - single-cell RNA-seq
